  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Confederation of Mongolian Trade Unions (CMTU) held discussions with its counterparts in the Central Asian region on outreach service delivery to the informal economy workers and conducted its internal reviews of their grievance management system and strategic plans in expanding service delivery and outreach in September and October 2023.  The proposals developed and adopted by the CMTU executive committee shall be pursued in 2024 as their strategic follow-through on workers&apos; activities and policy adaptation with the ILO and the greater UN system in Mongolia.
No data is yet available but CMTU has claimed gaining strength in the informal economy in Mongolia.  As a result of these efforts and CMTU coordination, some informal economy workers have managed to register and access social security benefits. The ILO provided technical support through online and in-person meetings in September and October 2023, technical reviews of documentation, and coordination with ILO departments on the design of the proposals adopted by CMTU in developing enhanced service provision.</narrative>
   </description>
